; Project-wide build policy, kept out of src/dune because it is not derived from
; any target and src/dune is generated from the project model.
;
; The tree still carries several hundred warnings, and dune's default flags mark
; their warnings fatal (the @ in -w @1..3@5..28...), so without this a build stops
; at the first one.
;
; Note that this only reaches stanzas which declare no (flags ...) field of their
; own: inside such a field, :standard means dune's defaults, not what is set here.
; Generated stanzas therefore carry -warn-error -A themselves, and this stanza
; covers the hand-written ones, dune.inc sections included.
(env (dev (flags (:standard -warn-error -A))))
